From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 02:01:42 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 198/342] media_server: a saved default of one type no longer
 blocks the others (M45)

DefaultManager::_FindPhysical() looked for the saved default of the type it
searches, but left msg pointing at the last saved one when none matched.
With only the audio output saved (HDMI), the video input, video output and
audio input were then compared with uninitialized data and none was ever
chosen: CodyCam found no video source although the C920's node was live.

usb_webcam: VideoProducer's destructor calls BMediaEventLooper::Quit()
first, as BMediaEventLooper asks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/add-ons/media/media-add-ons/usb_webcam/Producer.cpp | 3 +++
 src/servers/media/DefaultManager.cpp                    | 7 +++++--
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/media/media-add-ons/usb_webcam/Producer.cpp b/src/add-ons/media/media-add-ons/usb_webcam/Producer.cpp
index 606e2b84fa..bdee00917f 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/media/media-add-ons/usb_webcam/Producer.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/media/media-add-ons/usb_webcam/Producer.cpp
@@ -94,6 +94,9 @@ VideoProducer::VideoProducer(
 
 VideoProducer::~VideoProducer()
 {
+	// no more events while the node comes apart
+	BMediaEventLooper::Quit();
+
 	if (fInitStatus == B_OK) {
 		/* Clean up after ourselves, in case the application didn't make us
 		 * do so. */
diff --git a/src/servers/media/DefaultManager.cpp b/src/servers/media/DefaultManager.cpp
index 4132382691..7604c45b61 100644
--- a/src/servers/media/DefaultManager.cpp
+++ b/src/servers/media/DefaultManager.cpp
@@ -449,10 +449,13 @@ DefaultManager::_FindPhysical(volatile media_node_id *id, uint32 default_type,
 		|| (type == B_MEDIA_ENCODED_AUDIO);
 
 	for (int32 i = 0; i < fMsgList.CountItems(); i++) {
-		msg = (BMessage *)fMsgList.ItemAt(i);
+		BMessage* item = (BMessage *)fMsgList.ItemAt(i);
 		int32 msgType;
-		if (msg->FindInt32(kDefaultManagerType, &msgType) == B_OK
+		if (item->FindInt32(kDefaultManagerType, &msgType) == B_OK
 			&& ((uint32)msgType == default_type)) {
+			// only a saved default of this type limits the choice; with
+			// none, any physical node will do
+			msg = item;
 			const char *name = NULL;
 			const char *path = NULL;
 			msg->FindInt32(kDefaultManagerAddon, &msgDninfo.addon);
